; routeworld.eval - a patrol route does not outlive its world (code-review C233).
; Judged by tools/EditorTest.py phase 23, which makes the second scratch world
; this script switches to (et_next, a copy of the same world) and then checks
; every level file there is untouched.
;
; ONE `reset`, the one that loads the world: monster ids number from 1 in each
; world, and the same level loaded the same way hands out the same ids - so A's
; id names a live monster in et_next too, which is exactly how a stale route
; used to reach the next world's monster. A second reset would respawn, and
; renumber, before the inspect. The last section prints et_next's monster and
; its id, so the judge can see the collision was there to be had.
;
;   --- before ---  A (the skel_warrior at 23,9) gets a route with a waypoint.
;   --- after ---   in et_next: no route is being laid; on the player map (M)
;                   Esc is not the route's, no inspector opens, and its Save
;                   has nothing to save (it used to write et_next's .ent).
;   --- ids ---     et_next's skel_warrior and its id.

logecho on
reset
timescale 0
echo --- before ---
editor inspect 23 9
editor inspector
editor inspector editroute
editor route 23 11
editor route
worlds load et_next
echo --- after ---
timescale 0
editor route
mappage open
editor route key esc
editor inspector
editor inspector save
editor route
mappage close
echo --- ids ---
editor inspect 23 9
editor inspector
editor inspect off
echo --- end ---
